What are Template Engines in Express js ?
=======================================
→ Template engines are libraries that enable developers to generate dynamic HTML content by combining static HTML templates with data
Name some Template Engines libraries : 
EJS (Embedded JavaScript)
Pug (formerly Jade),Handlebars,Mustache,Nunjucks

Step by step Implementation : 
→npm init -y
→npm install express ejs
→project/
│
├── app.js
├── views/
│   └── index.ejs
└── package.json
→ const express = require("express");
const app = express();
// set EJS as template engine
app.set("view engine", "ejs");
// route
app.get("/", (req, res) => {  res.render("index", { name: "Aziz", role: "Backend Developer" });});
// start server
app.listen(3000, () => {  console.log("Server running on port 3000");});
Create EJS file (views/index.ejs)
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>EJS Example</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Hello <%= name %></h1>
  <p>Your role is: <%= role %></p>
</body>
</html>
